<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="BossaAntiqua-Bb-Theme" spTempo="140">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1964
Composer:	Paul Desmond
Lyricist:	None — instrumental
Form:	32-bar AABA
Style:	Bossa nova
Key:	Eb major

Paul Desmond composed “Bossa Antigua” for his 1964
recording sessions, and it appeared on the album Bossa
Antigua, released in 1964 or 1965 depending on the
cataloging source. The piece is an instrumental
Brazilian-inspired jazz composition whose title
humorously combines “bossa” with “antigua,” suggesting
an “old bossa”</spComments>
